.TH SCS-ACME-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "sslcrtsrv 0.8.4" "SSLCrtSrv Manual"
.SH NAME
scs-acme-server \- RFC 8555 ACME protocol server for SSLCrtSrv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scs-acme-server
.RI [ \-\-config " " PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scs-acme-server
is a second, independent listener that lets third-party ACME clients (e.g.
.BR certbot (1)
or
.BR acme.sh (1)
itself) request certificates through this server's own account/authorization
model, instead of the native
.BR scs-client (1)
protocol. It shares the same database as
.BR scs-server (1)
and the same
.I server_config.json
\(em there is no separate ACME-specific config file and no
.B init
subcommand of its own.
.PP
Run as its own long-lived process, typically behind a reverse proxy that
terminates TLS (see
.B acme_external_url
below) and forwards the ACME path prefix to
.BR scs-acme-server 's
plain-HTTP listener. It has nothing to do until
.B acme_enabled
is set to
.B true
in
.IR server_config.json ,
and refuses to start without it. See
.I ACME_SERVER_DESIGN.md
in the project source for the full protocol design and reverse-proxy
requirements.
.PP
Certificate issuance for orders placed through this server is still carried
out by
.BR scs-crtrequest (1),
which must be run (e.g. from cron) exactly as it already is for the native
protocol \(em no separate cron job is needed for ACME orders.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " PATH
Server config file to read
.B acme_*
settings, the database location, and notifier configuration from. Default
.IR /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json .
.SH CONFIGURATION
The following fields in
.I server_config.json
control this server; there is currently no CLI flag on
.B scs-acme-server
itself to set them \(em use
.BR scs-server (1)
.B init
or edit the file directly.
.TP
.B acme_enabled
Must be
.B true
for this process to start at all. Default
.IR false .
.TP
.B acme_external_url
Required whenever
.B acme_enabled
is
.BR true .
The externally-visible base URL of the ACME endpoint, behind the mandatory
reverse proxy \(em e.g.
.IR https://ca.example.com/acme .
Every ACME resource URL returned to clients is built from this, never from
request headers.
.TP
.B acme_listen
Local address this process binds to (behind the reverse proxy). Default
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B acme_port
Local port this process binds to. Default
.IR 5580 .
.TP
.B acme_trusted_proxy_ip
Optional. The reverse proxy's own address \(em when the direct TCP peer of a
request matches this exactly,
.B X-Forwarded-For
is trusted for IP-pinning enforcement (see
.BR scs-cltmanager (1)'s
.B set_allowed_ip
command); otherwise
.B X-Forwarded-For
is never consulted, regardless of what a client sends. Default
.IR unset ,
meaning IP-pinning (if any account has it configured) always checks the
direct TCP peer address only.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json
\(em default configuration file, shared with
.BR scs-server (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scs-server (1),
.BR scs-crtrequest (1),
.BR scs-cltmanager (1)
.PP
.I ACME_SERVER_DESIGN.md
in the project source has the full protocol design and rationale.
.SH AUTHOR
Garry Glendown
